Description: Design of area and list sample surveys that go to the field,
    minimising the real cost of field work (travel between sampling units
    plus interviews) subject to a target variance of the design-based
    estimator. Travel matrices from coordinates or a road network, GRASP
    routing of the field work for one or several teams, spatially balanced
    selection of units with the local pivotal method, Horvitz-Thompson
    estimation with the local-mean variance estimator, cost-aware
    allocation across strata or frames, and the cost-variance frontier of
    a design by simulation. The computational engine is the Rust crate
    fieldopt-core.
